{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01005 - MONDO_20543",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxyurea appears to be linked to Theca Steroid-producing Cell Malignant Tumor Of Ovary, Not Further Specified through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Hydroxyurea is associated with Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary and Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma, both of which are indicated to lead to the target tumor type. This implies that Hydroxyurea may exert some form of therapeutic or pathophysiological effect that influences the development or progression of these ovarian tumors. The presence of multiple pathways involving different drugs (Melphalan, Belotecan, and Tretamine) further supports the idea that Hydroxyurea could be part of a broader mechanism that interacts with these malignancies. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Hydroxyurea to play a role in the pathogenesis of Theca Steroid-producing Cell Malignant Tumor Of Ovary, Not Further Specified, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
